// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - ArbiterRichard 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P1792580116" "What is it that you want, citizen?  I am not required to speak with you unless you feel you need training.  Out with it, already!"
// Answer Text :
"P2061251617" "So, umm... You're a trainer, right?"
// Page RichardOne Text :
"P1330032375" "What kind of foolish question is that?  Of course I'm a trainer!<br><br><color orange>Arbiter Richard stares at you with extreme annoyance.</color><br><br>Hold on a moment... You're {HeroName}, are you not?  You've already been granted the right to increase your powers several times now.  As a matter of fact, I believe I may even have granted you that right personally.  What is this all about?"
// Answer Text :
"P2261632408" "I don't remember... I think I may have been, um, mindwiped."
// Page RichardTwo Text :
"P1746293602" "Mindwiped?  I'm unaware of any local individual who has been authorized use of those powers, let alone deign to use them on you.  Now speak up!  Who was it that mindwiped you?"
// Answer Text :
"P2652019754" "I don't remember.  I was mindwiped, remember?"
// Page RichardThree Text :
"P292385733" "How convenient.  Alright then.  I'll play along... For now.<br><br><color orange>Arbiter Richard glares at you.</color><br><br>To answer your original question, yes... I'm a trainer.  An arbiter, to be exact.  You will come to me when you feel you can demonstrate increased powers through undertaking tasks that please Arachnos and Lord Recluse.  If you can exhibit enough gained experience I, or another Arbiter, may judge you worthy of the privilege of increasing your powers."
// Answer Text :
"P3543740331" "I forgot what experience means."
// Page RichardFour Text :
"P3904669420" "WHAT?!  How could you forget something as simple as that?  Experience is gained by combating those that Arachnos deems an enemy.  Or by undertaking special missions, as well.  Only a simpleton would ask such a ridiculous question!<br><br>...oh yes... I forgot...<br><br>You've been mindwiped."
// Answer Text :
"P3440669762" "Oh no!  Maybe you've been mindwiped, too?"
// Page RichardDone Text :
"P442545887" "I HAVE NOT -- <br><br><color orange>Arbiter Richard visciously snarls as if he is seriously considering striking you.  After a deep breath, he regains his composure.</color><br><br>I have an idea... let me help you, {HeroName}.   I want you to go speak with Arbiter Unger in Port Oakes.  I'm quite certain he will be more than happy to answer any and every question you have for him.  Please be sure to ask him, oh I don't know, any little thing you're even the slightest bit curious about.  Perhaps you would like to know why the sky is blue?  Well then, you be sure to ask, alright?  That'll be fun, won't it?<br><br>Travel south beyond the wall until you arrive at the Ferry at which point you can take it to Port Oakes West.  Now... leave my presence...<br><br>Immediately."
// Answer Text :
"P49815073" "Thank you so much for your help, Arbiter.  Have a nice day!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - ArbiterUnger 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P2898212980" "Citizen.  If you are standing before me, that must only mean you are claiming your right to increase your powers?  You in no way would be here to waste my time, am I right?  I mean...<br><br>That would be quite dangerous, wouldn't you agree?"
// Answer Text :
"P1547880885" "Actually, Arbiter Richard directed me to you."
// Page UngerOne Text :
"P4198486389" "Oh he did now, did he?  What is it that you need from me that he could not deal with himself?"
// Answer Text :
"P1532628849" "I wanted to know how the Ferries worked."
// Page UngerTwo Text :
"P1882856234" "You wanted to know how the ferries work...<br><br>And he sent you to me.  To ask me 'how the ferries' work.<br><br>Let me make sure I understand this correctly.  Arbiter Richard, rather than answer this pathetic question himself, sent you to ME.  And he very specifically said, to you, that you were to speak to Arbiter Unger... am I understanding this right?"
// Answer Text :
"P1923497608" "No sir... He said 'speak to that brown-nosing Unger'."
// Page UngerThree Text :
"P2792979652" "...Brown... nosing?...<br><br><color orange>Arbiter Unger clenches his teeth.</color><br><br>I see.  Very well.  I'll answer your question, citizen.<br><br>The ferries are but one means of transportation throughout the islands that make up the Rogue Isles.  By the grace the of Lord Recluse, these ferries are free to use and will take you to a number of different ports.  You can use them any time you wish, reducing the time it would take to travel there through conventional means.<br><br>Know this.  Although Arachnos has provided you the means of transportation, we do not provide you protection in your journeys.  If you wander into a neighborhood with individuals far more powerful than you, your body will be unceremoniously dumped into the ocean.<br><br>Similar to what I have in mind for Richard when I next see him."
// Answer Text :
"P3659180400" "You're going to kill him?  Are Arbiters allowed to do that?"
// Page UngerDone Text :
"P3647699303" "What?  Oh no, you mistake me.  I would never lay a hand upon one of my fellow Arbiters, even a buffoon the likes of Richard.<br><br>However, I understand he is still dealing with the problem of a corrupt police force within his purview.  Were the Rogue Isles Police force to start winding up in the hospital after a spate of mysterious attacks... well, I'm quite certain their Police Chief will want answers from Richard personally...<br><br>And when that's all done, I'd be curious to see whose nose is browner.<br><br>Now then... I've answered your question.  Unless you have real business with me, I would suggest that you go about your day - somewhere - else."
// Answer Text :
"P2977033756" "I understand.  I'll be on my way now."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3337450449" "{HeroName}.  Before the first round of the competition begins, we must be certain that the everpresent grasp of Arachnos has not taken notice of our... festivities.   Thus, I have assigned each of you the task of reducing your profile - your importance, if you will - in the eyes of those who govern the pecking order in the Rogue Isles.<br><br>In other words, make the Arbiters believe you're not someone worth paying attention to for the time being."
// AcceptString :
"P1276734209" "If I must.  What exactly do I need to do?"
// SendOffString :
"P1624487994" "You have most likely already spoken with the arbiters that grant you permission to increase your powers.  Although they appear to regard you as just one of the teeming throng that litter the streets of Mercy Island, this is not truly the case.  I would suspect they have already taken a silent interest towards your activities, making your movements not as slight as you may believe.<br><br>You will need to make them think you're not worth considering for the time being.  As part of your challenge, I will leave the details up to you.  However, if I were to offer a suggestion, perhaps you may want to convince them that you're woefully inexperienced.<br><br><color orange>Dr. Graves pauses for a moment as he reads your face.</color><br><br>In other words, tell them you're a 'noob'."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P3517858258" "<color deepskyblue>Undisciplined Disciple</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission2_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1432869697" "Talk to Arbiter Richard in Mercy Island"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2734703887" "What is delaying you, {HeroName}.  Distract the Arbiter by making him believe you are of no consequence!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1742330223" "You've managed to successfully annoy Arbiter Richard enough that he directed you to speak with Arbiter Unger in Port Oakes.  By his reaction, it sounds as if there's some type of feud between them, which will most definitely be taken advantage of.  You will need to take the Ferry to reach him."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission2_Part2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3464895020" "Go take a ride on the Ferry to Port Oakes West"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2058108201" "Hmmm... You've been effective at distracting one of Arbiters.  Now do as he said and arrive at the Ferry so that you can ride to Port Oakes West."
// VolumeDescription :
"P104483105" "Use your map to find the Rogue Isles Ferry"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1946933602" "You've reached the Rogue Isles Ferry leading out of Mercy Island.  Take a trip to Port Oakes West and find Arbiter Unger in the the Arena District."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission2_Part3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1834001630" "Talk to Arbiter Unger"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P842367461" "You should be able to find Arbiter Unger in the Arena District.  The Arena District is in the southern region of Port Oakes."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3195652291" "After speaking with Arbiter Unger, you've come up with a plan to create a distraction amongst the Arbiters.  If this works, they'll be too busy arguing amongst themselves to pay attention to you or the others' whereabouts. Travel back to Mercy Island and attack the corrupt cops that make up the Rogue Isles police force."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission2_Part4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3301534534" "Assault the corrupt cops in Mercy Island"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2469504161" "Although your idea is rather effective, this is not what you've been instructed to do.  However, if you insist, I will not get in your way of inflicting grevious bodily harm upon those hypocritical authoritarians.  You should find more than enough of them at Darwin's Landing or in Mercy City."
// VillainDescription :
"P3742173531" "Defeat {Remain} Rogue Isles Policemen"
// VillainSingularDescription :
"P2280858120" "One last corrupt policeman remains"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1296494997" "You have successfully beaten down enough cops to keep the Arbiters busy for a while.  Now it's time to inform Dr. Graves of your success."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2615938217" "I'm not sure what was going through your head when you decided to raise the ire of the Rogue Island Police, {HeroName}.  This runs directly counter-intuitive from your directions to reduce your profile.<br><br>You have, however, managed to keep the eyes of the police off of our activities; perhaps even Arachnos, themselves.  Because of this, I will not request that our faceless benefactor disqualify you... this time."
// RandomFameString :
"P3834130123" "Nice work on those cops, {HeroName}.  Those pigs totally deserved it."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - Mission3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - SecurityTerminal 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P2290005852" "<color orange>The console screen reads as follows:</color><br><br>All candidates will register.  Upon registration, the rules of the contest shall be provided.<br><br>The candidate will remain still for retinal scan."
// Answer Text :
"P1567117768" "Await retinal scan."
// Page FirstFloor Text :
"P205390362" "<color orange>From the top of the terminal, a device emerges that appears to be a robotic hand with a cylindrical end point.  A small hole is in the end of the cylinder which emits a small laser-dot.  The robotic hand scans the dot up your face, reaching the bridge of your eyes... and keeps moving upwards past your eyes until resting directly in the center of your forehead.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P4113480091" "Quickly move away from the laser!"
// Page SecondFloor Text :
"P415644111" "<color orange>You deftly move out of the way of the dot! <br><br>A split second later, the cylinder erupts forward a deadly laser blast where a moment earlier your head was.  Upon the screen lists the words:</color><br><br><color red>Analyzing Reaction Patterns<br><br>Dodge Rating: 0.32<br><br>Complacency Rating: 1.25<br><br>Submissiveness Rating: 5</color><br><br>Identity Confirmed: {HeroName}.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P3884338149" "Submissiveness Rating of 5?  Is that good or bad?!"
// Page ThirdFloor Text :
"P1015620294" "<color red>Candidate Registration Accepted<br><br>Message from Dr. Todd Graves directed to  {HeroName}:</color><br><br>{HeroName}, once again you have managed to survive this test.  However, as before, do not not laud yourself in victory laurels just yet.  From this moment forward your task will be to reach the corresponding terminal found hidden within this compound.  Once you have done so, you will enter the following code - Omega Zero Terminus."
// Answer Text :
"P3019951632" "Memorize the code."
// Page LockDown Text :
"P2815801881" "The trial will be judged by our benefactor through hidden eyes.  You will be judged not only by what place you reach the end, but also by what means you take to reach that end.<br><br>One final note: You are still under restrictions that prevent you from killing your fellow contestants.  'Accidents' will be fully investigated, and the perpetrator of those actions will be disqualilfied immediately with extreme prejudice."
// Answer Text :
"P2999231776" "Look for the other terminal before anyone else does!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - ZephyrPetOne 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P2850118396" "Why did it have to be skeletons?  I haaaaaate skeletons!!!<br><br>Ummm... can I stick around near you?"
// Answer Text :
"P2342969448" "You can't be serious, Zephyr.  They're not even really skeletons, you know."
// Page ConvoNode1 Text :
"P2420430154" "I don't care, man!  When I, uh, made my, um, first body - yeah, that's it - I, uh, forgot to make a skeleton for it, right?  So then I -- don't laugh at me!<br><br>Crosscut laughed at me and, man, I tell you... that was even creepier than these skeleton guys!"
// Answer Text :
"P400830793" "You're seriously afraid of skeletons?  That is the most ridiculous thi --"
// Page ConvoNode2 Text :
"P2003998377" "Look, man.  If you keep making fun of me for that, I'll go back and hang out next to Crosscut.  But since he's further ahead of you, it looks like you'll have to beat BOTH of us, okay?<br><br>On the other hand, you can shut up with the mocking and I'll chill out with you... giving you a better chance at winning this round... see where I'm going with this?"
// Answer Text :
"P1583411390" "Hmmm... very well.  You say Crosscut was up ahead?"
// Page ConvoNode3 Text :
"P3097871005" "Yeah, he was just around the corner fighting some of those skeleton dudes.  He didn't really seem like he was in a rush, though.  To be honest, I think he was more interested in playing with them than actually winning this round."
// Answer Text :
"P784478254" "Then I'll encourage him to keep up the good work..."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - CrosscutPetOne 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P2424083153" "I've been trying to get them to say trick or treat for the past hour, and not one of these little spookies will play along.<br><br>Now what ever am I to do with my nifty trick I had planned for them?"
// Answer Text :
"P4194702603" "I'm afraid to ask, but what was this trick?"
// Page ConversationNode1 Text :
"P1391510891" "I have this earpiece that lets me talk over the unused intercom system.  It's like the little bird that sits on your windowsill that you tell all of your secrets to.<br><br>But this little bird tells your secrets to everyone here.  My trick was to tell everyone my secrets... some of my dirty, dirty secrets...<br><br>Can I tell you my secrets, {HeroName}?  Oh please... let me breathe my secrets into your ear..."
// Answer Text :
"P1776814896" "If you give me that earpiece and tell me how to use it, I'll think about it."
// Page ConversationNode2 Text :
"P3402993899" "Ohhh... I will like telling them to you.  Just me and you... alone... sharing my secrets with you...<br><br>Here is the earpiece.  All you do is say your secrets into the mic. Then, when you think it's the perfect time to drip your secrets inside everyone, you just say - 'Open Wide'.  You will first need to override the system, but that should be easy enough.<br><br>Now... let me think... what secrets should I tell you?  Maybe I'll tell you about the bad things I've done with seat belts?  Or with the doggy door?  Ah... the retirement party... I've never told <b>anyone</b> where <b>all</b> of them went... yesssss... that one..."
// Answer Text :
"P1939420088" "I said MAYBE I'll let you!  Remember that, Crosscut!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - GravesPetOne 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P1301667910" "I am here to confirm the winner of this first round, and as you are able to see, Dollface has beaten each of you to the finish line.  All that is left is for the winner to register their name in the Endpoint Marker--"
// Answer Text :
"P1720579562" "Stop right there!"
// Page ConversationNode1 Text :
"P1244691180" "I do not know what you mean accomplish by delaying the inevitable, {HeroName}, but Dollface is clearly the winner.  If you attempt to stop her by force, I will respond in kind <b>and</b> disqualify you from the contest."
// Answer Text :
"P3356598501" "I know the rules, Graves.  I just wanted to congratulate her by saying 'open wide'."
// Page ConversationNode2 Text :
"P3015669785" "Open wide?  What foolish nonsense is--<br><br><color orange>Dr. Graves looks in the direction of the speakers.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P1100755604" "Sorry, but it's a secret."
// Page ConversationNode3 Text :
"P2371474499" "<color orange>Dr. Graves quickly looks at Dollface.</color>"
// Answer Text :
"P3444938998" "Wow... looks like you get a lot of cars, Dollface!  You'd better hurry and get them!"
// Page ConversationNode4 Text :
"P956864995" "I had no involvement with that message in any way or form!<br><br><color orange>Dr. Graves turns his eyes upon you.</color><br><br>However, I have a good mind as to who might be responsible for that highly coincidental announcement."
// Answer Text :
"P1613284959" "I'd love to hear your thoughts.  But first, I'm going to win."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog - SecurityTerminalTwo 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Page Intro Text :
"P3849474689" "<color orange>The terminal has only one line blinking on the screen.</color><br><br>Enter Victory Code."
// Answer Text :
"P3063876776" "TYPE: Omega Zero Terminus."
// Page ConversationNode1 Text :
"P694247935" "<color orange>The screen pauses for a moment then displays the following:</color><br><br><color red>Round One Victor:</color><br><br>{HeroName}"
// Answer Text :
"P2982239551" "Looks like the round is over, Graves."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P509053332" "It is now time for the trials to begin.  This shall be the first of several competitive events that will be used to gauge your strengths, and potentially cull the weak.  Let us hope for your sake that you are not the first to be culled."
// AcceptString :
"P180917318" "That will never happen.  When does this trial begin?"
// SendOffString :
"P2062502151" "While you and the rest were avoiding the eye of Arachnos, I have put into motion all of the situations you will encounter and be judged by.  You and the others will return to the impromptu training-grounds  and utilize the registration terminal to begin the competetion.  The first to the finish line will be determined as the winner of Round One.<br><br>Oh, and you may wish to hurry.  For you see, the competition has already begun..."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1301475953" "Beat the other Contestants!"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3171326117" "I would highly suggest that you graced us with your presence in the Trial Grounds, {HeroName}.  The longer you wait, the more you have given your fellow competitors that much more headway towards the finish line."
// TaskSubTitle :
"P3298888516" "<color deepskyblue>Skeletons in Your Warehouse</color>"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// MissionDef 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// EntryString :
"P4214344899" "You can hear various yells and explosion sounds coming from deeper inside the building.  It looks like you may have gotten here too late!"
// Script Variable ObjectiveUIText :
"P604562539" "Trick Zephyr into following you!"
// Script Variable ObjectiveUIText :
"P1386624237" "Trick Crosscut into following you!"
// Script Variable ObjectiveUIText :
"P545708355" "Find the Marker before the others do!"
// Script Variable ObjectiveUIText :
"P3463877626" "QUICKLY!  Use the Marker!!!"
// Script Variable ObjectiveUIText :
"P4250922850" "Deal with the angry Skulls!"
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P1259260415" "Skull Opportunist"
// Script Variable BOSS_INACTIVE_DIALOG :
"P3169570349" "So alls I gotta do is beat up one of these supers and I'll get the cash?"
// Script Variable BOSS_ATTACK_DIALOG :
"P3940450028" "Oh yeah... here's another one now!"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P2836457115" "Now you die!"
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYNAME :
"P2774141083" "Trial Marker"
// Script Variable BOSS_DISPLAYINFO :
"P1154403306" "This computer will register the candidate's entry."
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P3193922572" "<t=5 caption x= 0.2 y=0.2 d=5><scale 1.75><color darkgray><bgcolor black>Candidate Omnicore.  Due to your speed in this trial, you are under suspicion of tampering with the Trial Marker.<t=5 caption x= 0.2 y=0.4 d=5><scale 1.75><color darkgray><bgcolor black>You are hereby obligated to join with {HeroName} in the earlier sections of the trial grounds. <t=5 caption x= 0.2 y=0.2 d=5><scale 1.75><color darkgray><bgcolor black>Any objections on your part will result in your disqualification.  {HeroName} has no tolerance to your whining, so you had better keep your mouth shut, got it?!"
// Script Variable SaysList :
"P2154564238" "<t=5 caption x= 0.2 y=0.2 d=5><scale 1.75><color darkgray><bgcolor black>This message is intended for all of you suckers with your silly skull facepaint.<t=5 caption x= 0.2 y=0.4 d=5><scale 1.75><color darkgray><bgcolor black>All of the riches that you were promised will now be given to the winner of the trial at the entrance to these testing grounds.<t=5 caption x= 0.2 y=0.2 d=5><scale 1.75><color darkgray><bgcolor black>I hate to say, but you were all going to be given a new car.  The winner gets to have all the cars.  And a lot of money.  And they get to be famous, too.<t=5 caption x= 0.2 y=0.2 d=5><scale 1.75><color darkgray><bgcolor black>Tough luck, suckers!"

